                <pb facs="0189" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1428</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-04T23:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1918,
                                11 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 5, 5.50 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At 11 o’clock a.m., five armed Russians entered Japanese office in central
                    district this city, demanded money, and when refused shot three Japanese killing
                    one and seriously wounding others.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caldwell</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
